            "dataset": "soter_polygons",
            "source_code": "totc",
            "source_notes": "Values as stored in the SOTER database of each dataset, represented at 7 significant digits (binary storage tails removed); the extracted value is kept unchanged in the raw layer. The 4-letter column codes are not defined in any retrieved ISRIC document: the manual items cited here are matched to the column by its name and by the fill rates of the dataset reports (inference documented in docs/inventory/soter-source-fields.md). M95 item 110 (p.57) defines TOTC as 'total organic carbon'; M13 item 130 (p.75) as total carbon (organic + inorganic), with organic carbon as item 131 (ORGC). Mapped per dataset documentation (decision on #54): Malawi (2013 structure; ISRIC Report 2016/01, p.16 lists 'total carbon' and 'organic carbon') TOTC = total carbon; the other 12 datasets TOTC = organic carbon (the reports of SOTERSAF, SOTERLAC, Nepal and Upper Tana call it total organic carbon). One SOTERLAC value is 989 g/kg; published as in the source. Kenya (KENSOTER) and Upper Tana give values for profiles with 'syn' in PRID: 'synthetic profiles' for which 'all 18 parameter estimates have been derived via taxotransfer or using expert estimates' (ISRIC Report 2004/01, p.10, p.14), 'virtual profiles, for which there are no measured soil data' (ISRIC Report 2010/09, p.11); every row of such a profile carries source_profile_type (synthetic or virtual)."
          }
