            "dataset": "soter_polygons",
            "source_code": "p2o5",
            "source_notes": "Values as stored in the SOTER database of each dataset, represented at 7 significant digits (binary storage tails removed); the extracted value is kept unchanged in the raw layer. The 4-letter column codes are not defined in any retrieved ISRIC document: the manual items cited here are matched to the column by its name and by the fill rates of the dataset reports (inference documented in docs/inventory/soter-source-fields.md). M95 item 112 (p.57): 'the P2O5 content in mg kg-1', no method; M13 splits available P (item 133) and total P (item 134), mg kg-1 (p.75). Mapped per dataset documentation (decision on #54): SOTERSAF profiles with PRID prefix AO (Angola, 314 values) to total phosphorus ('the given P2O5 contents for Angola are the total phosphate contents', ISRIC SOTERSAF report 2003, p.12); Malawi and Upper Tana (2013 structure) to available phosphorus; all other values to P2O5 content, method unspecified. China: values about 100 times higher than most datasets (median 500 mg/kg, 4,656 of 4,872 above 100), unexplained by the documents; published as in the source. Zero values may stand for absent or not determined: the SOTER manual asks to leave unmeasured values empty (M13 p.20) and no field marks which zeros were measured; published as in the source."
          }
